{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-extended-idle-single-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.41, step 7f: `process-extended-idle-single`, Total Energy Consumption from EXTENDED IDLE (9190) for the combination long-haul truck at Washtenaw County SINGLE scale, computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE plus the run's COUNTY input database. It mounts `inputs/washtenaw-county-hotelling.esm`, which declares the county database's rows and the SINGLE domain and mounts the default database; that and the selections below are the whole of the difference from a DEFAULT-domain run.\n\nWHAT THE MODEL DOES FOR IT, none of it written here: the activity is TotalActivityGenerator's hotelling hours (`hot_hours`) -- the truck's daily VMT on the restricted-access road types x the zone's ROW-MERGED SHOAllocFactor x hotellingRate, spread over the hours by hotellingdist and rescaled by AdjustHotelling to the county's hotellingHoursPerDay -- in place of SHO; the operating-mode weight is RatesOperatingModeDistributionGenerator step 200's degenerate distribution, mode 200 at 1, times BaseRateCalculator's hourFractionAdjust from the ROW-MERGED hotellingActivityDistribution at the best zone the merged table holds (261610, the county's own); and the rows live on road type 1, the off-network one, where the RunSpec's second road type puts them.\n\n`n_outputRate` IS 50: one block, 41 diesel model years and the 9 CNG ones that have an extended-idle rate. `run_domainUnported` and `run_selectionUnported` are 0.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
